{"id": "EUVD-2026-93289", "enisaUuid": "b0208372-a20d-3e8f-9861-f9becfbcb3b7", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: bcmgenet: restore the hardware filters on open\n\nbcmgenet_hfb_init() runs INIT_LIST_HEAD() on priv->rxnfc_list, which drops\nevery rule off the list, and bcmgenet_open() calls it on each ifup. Every\nrule the user configured is silently lost:\n\n  # ethtool -N eth0 flow-type ether dst $MAC action 0\n  Added rule with ID 0\n  # ethtool -n eth0 | grep -c Filter:\n  1\n  # ip link set eth0 down && ip link set eth0 up\n  # ethtool -n eth0 | grep -c Filter:\n  0\n\nInitialise the lists once at probe and restore the rules on open, as\nbcmgenet_resume() already does.", "datePublished": "2026-10-06T08:46:01", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:17:15", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/56db7ec462d6a2b886e299ad835109c089606969", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/906140955c8debde65afe12e594e04c49a61b0d9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/23ca4ddc4fce2c233a49e9fd34d4b5b02bd7324e"], "aliases": ["GHSA-3cc5-5jg6-g6px", "CVE-2026-98304"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0c60753b-1e2f-3a73-af4a-b7077b0d1076", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3e370952287c55e5fd240cb8bb41ef8acff8829d <56db7ec462d6a2b886e299ad835109c089606969"}, {"id": "285add19-ef47-3826-9968-f2dc6cff3885", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.54"}, {"id": "656a1048-b4fb-32ea-95ba-9dd361622930", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.8"}, {"id": "72423482-1410-32b7-b371-d92ff3dab558", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "8477a604-c802-36d2-90d5-09460db8e9f9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.8"}, {"id": "8e85cdb0-71ff-37c2-ac57-bf8261d4b2